{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"openSUSE-SU-2026:21973-1","published":"2026-09-29T16:29:51Z","modified":"2026-10-01T18:23:09.938455446Z","related":["CVE-2026-93586","CVE-2026-93587","CVE-2026-93588","CVE-2026-93589","CVE-2026-93590"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-93586","CVE-2026-93587","CVE-2026-93588","CVE-2026-93589","CVE-2026-93590"],"summary":"Security update for ImageMagick","details":"This update for ImageMagick fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-93586: use-after-free in the `ImagesToBlob` method can lead to a process crash (bsc#1281912).\n- CVE-2026-93587: policy bypass in the PCD, CUBE and HALD coders can lead to extra memory allocation and a denial of\n  service (bsc#1281909).\n- CVE-2026-93588: NULL pointer dereference in the PNM coder can lead to a denial of service (bsc#1281910).\n- CVE-2026-93589: division-by-zero flaw in the FLIF encoder can lead to a denial of service (bsc#1281911).\n- CVE-2026-93590: failure to perform policy checks during buffer allocation for image pixels in the UHDR encoder can\n  lead to denial of service (bsc#1281913).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"ImageMagick","ecosystem":"openSUSE:Leap 16.0","purl":"pkg:rpm/opensuse/ImageMagick&distro=openSUSE%20Leap%2016.0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"7.1.2.0-160000.16.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"ImageMagick":"7.1.2.0-160000.16.1","ImageMagick-config-7-SUSE":"7.1.2.0-160000.16.1","ImageMagick-config-7-upstream-limited":"7.1.2.0-160000.16.1","ImageMagick-config-7-upstream-open":"7.1.2.0-160000.16.1","ImageMagick-config-7-upstream-secure":"7.1.2.0-160000.16.1","ImageMagick-config-7-upstream-websafe":"7.1.2.0-160000.16.1","ImageMagick-devel":"7.1.2.0-160000.16.1","ImageMagick-doc":"7.1.2.0-160000.16.1","ImageMagick-extra":"7.1.2.0-160000.16.1","libMagick++-7_Q16HDRI5":"7.1.2.0-160000.16.1","libMagick++-devel":"7.1.2.0-160000.16.1","libMagickCore-7_Q16HDRI10":"7.1.2.0-160000.16.1","libMagickWand-7_Q16HDRI10":"7.1.2.0-160000.16.1","perl